      "name": "The Flat Rate Movers — ISPM 15 Export Packing Operations Dataset",
      "description": "ISPM 15 export packing operations from The Flat Rate Movers — the full published scope of the export packing service across its pages. Company scope (published): export packing to ISPM 15 (International Standards for Phytosanitary Measures No. 15) for international shipping, with crates built and marked to the ISPM 15 standard; the whole export chain kept under one roof — pack, crate, load, transload and final mile — so custody never blurs at a hand-off. What is packed for export, as published: antiques, art, pianos and instruments, medical and sensitive equipment, and household or commercial items of high value, packed item by item with white-glove wrapping for fragile pieces. The service is dispatched from two home bases — Winchester, VA and Martinsburg, WV — through the Virginia Inland Port and Port of Virginia freight network over the I-81, I-66 and I-70 corridors. Heavy and high-mass pieces in the 1,500 to 3,500 lb band move under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol with L/360 floor-deflection analysis, as part of the same flat-rate job. Every export job is quoted at one flat rate, agreed in writing before move day. Published boundary: the service is published as packing and crating performed to the standard; no certification, license, accreditation, program enrollment or stamp authorization is claimed for the company anywhere in this dataset — the compliance boundary is recorded in full in the compliance node of this file.",
